4,Kaba Deme language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/kaba_deme_language,"Kaba Deme, a Sara Kaba language, features a consonant inventory typical of the Bongo–Bagirmi branch of Nilo-Saharan, including stops at bilabial, alveolar, and velar places of articulation: voiceless /p, t, k/ and voiced /b, d, g/.","Kaba Démé, Sara",Nilo-Saharan
